Z||000000||jeffndebrus||08-14-2001||11:17 PM||||Please help if you can.<BR>I am the proud new owner of a 85 se with the 2.8 v6.  Apparently the most recent owner parked it because it kept fraying belts and throwing them about every two weeks.  This became frustrating so the car was parked.  It starts and runs smoothly and i am most exited at the thought of my first drive in it but will have to figure out what is the problem before I can drive it.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bluebottlejunky||08-14-2001||11:20 PM||||Well mine was fraying because my alternator was tilted..and witch in the long run ended up spinning a bearing and need a new alternator..so make sure the alt isnt tilted..<P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||08-14-2001||11:39 PM||||my 85GT was shredding belts a while back, replace the alt.....  It was seizing cause it failed  causing too much tension so it just slips then eats the belt||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierohoho||08-15-2001||09:40 AM||||I would pull the belt then manually turn each pulley by hand and feel for any binding or resistance with the alternator and all the pulleys.<P>Also feel the pulleys and try a visual inspection for any rusted and rough areas which could cause premature wear.<P>Godd luck<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000004||hyhy4u||08-15-2001||01:35 PM||||My alternator was tilted because the upper "U" braket was stripped causing the bolt to come out somewhat making the alternator tilt pertty bad..this caused mine to have a terrible noise but never really caused any damage..If that is the case just go get a new alternator bolt and bring it completly throught the braket and throw a bolt on the end..mines been good ever since!||||reg||1
